---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import SearchFieldDemo from '../../components/SearchFieldDemo';
---

<Docs
  title="Search Field"
  description="A controlled search input with a magnifier and a clear button, for filtering lists, pickers, and catalogs."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Search Field</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A search input with a magnifier and a clear button. Use it to filter a page list, a picker, or a catalog.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <SearchFieldDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Search Field usage"
      code={`import { SearchField } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/search-field";

const [search, setSearch] = useState("");

<SearchField
  id="agent-search"
  label="Find agents"
  placeholder="Search agents"
  maxLength={120}
  value={search}
  onChange={setSearch}
/>

// Placeholder falls back to the label.
<SearchField label="Search models" value={query} onChange={setQuery} />`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Props</h2>
    <p>
      <code>label</code> names the input for screen readers. It is also the placeholder when you leave out{' '}
      <code>placeholder</code>.<code>value</code> and <code>onChange</code> are required;
      <code>onChange</code> gets the new string, not an event. Reset paging or cursors in it when the search changes.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>maxLength</code> and <code>id</code> pass to the input. Cloud uses 120 for agents, skills, tasks, and
      actions; 254 for invitations; 255 for tables, projects, files, and rows; 500 for Google Drive; and 640 for chats.{' '}
      <code>className</code> goes on the wrapper, which is full width up to 24rem. Put it in a flex child to size it in
      a toolbar.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is one size, 32px tall, and no variants. To disable it, wrap it in a disabled <code>fieldset</code>; the
      input and clear button both turn off.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Behavior</h2>
    <p>
      The clear button shows once there is text. It empties the value and puts focus back in the input. Escape does the
      same while there is text, and stops there, so a popover or dialog stays open. With no text, Escape passes through
      and closes them. Clicking the magnifier or padding focuses the input. Inside a form, Enter submits.
    </p>
    <p>
      The input is a native <code>type="search"</code>. The browser's own cancel button is hidden, so there is one clear
      button in every browser. Autocomplete and spell check are off.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The input is named by <code>label</code>, and the clear button is named "Clear search". The group shows a 2px
      focus ring when the input has keyboard focus; the clear button has its own ring. Show loading, error, and result
      counts in a status or alert region next to the field.
    </p>
    <p>
      The clear button fades in over 120ms. Motion and color transitions stop when reduced motion is requested. In
      forced colors mode the group keeps a system border and a highlight focus ring.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The border uses <code>--sprout-input</code>, the fill
      <code>--sprout-surface</code>, text <code>--sprout-text</code>, and the icon and placeholder{' '}
      <code>--sprout-muted</code>. Focus uses
      <code>--sprout-focus</code> and disabled <code>--sprout-hover</code>. Radius follows{' '}
      <code>--sprout-radius-control</code>. The opt-in TulipFarm theme tints the focus ring through these tokens.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
